---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout
	title="Bibliografía y fuentes documentales — Ars Cantorum"
	description="Catálogo bibliográfico de Ars Cantorum: tratados históricos del Bel Canto, pedagogía vocal, acústica y ciencia de la voz, dicción y musicología."
	ogType="website"
>
	<div class="container" style="max-width: 800px;">
		<div class="font-sans" style="margin-bottom: 2rem;">
			<a href="/" style="display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: 0.4rem; color: #64748b; font-size: 0.9rem; font-weight: 500;">
				← Volver a la biblioteca de ensayos
			</a>
		</div>

		<header style="margin-bottom: 3rem; padding-bottom: 2rem; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border-color);">
			<div class="font-sans" style="font-size: 0.75rem; font-weight: 700; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.08em; background: #f4ede3; color: var(--accent-gold); display: inline-block; padding: 0.2rem 0.65rem; border-radius: 4px; margin-bottom: 0.65rem;">
				Catálogo Documental
			</div>
			<h1 style="font-size: 2.3rem; color: #0f172a; line-height: 1.2; margin-bottom: 0.6rem;">
				Bibliografía y fuentes primarias
			</h1>
			<p style="font-size: 1.15rem; color: #475569; font-style: italic; line-height: 1.6;">
				Tratados históricos del Bel Canto, pedagogía vocal comparada, ciencia acústica y estudios musicológicos que sustentan los ensayos de Ars Cantorum.
			</p>
		</header>

		<div class="biblio-contenido" style="display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 2.4rem; font-size: 1.08rem; line-height: 1.75; color: #1e293b;">
			<section>
				<h2 class="biblio-h2">1. Tratados históricos y métodos clásicos (siglos XVI–XIX)</h2>
				<ul class="biblio-list">
					<li><strong>Giovanni Battista Bovicelli</strong>, <em>Regole, passaggi di musica</em> (1594)</li>
					<li><strong>Giulio Caccini</strong>, <em>Le Nuove Musiche</em> (1601)</li>
					<li><strong>Francesco Rognoni</strong>, <em>Selva de varii passaggi</em> (1620, Libros I y II)</li>
					<li><strong>Bénigne de Bacilly</strong>, <em>Remarques curieuses sur l'art de bien chanter</em> (1668)</li>
					<li><strong>Pier Francesco Tosi</strong>, <em>Opinioni de' cantori antichi, e moderni</em> (1723) / <em>Observations on the Florid Song</em> (ed. Galliard, 1743)</li>
					<li><strong>Jean-Antoine Bérard</strong>, <em>L'Art du chant</em> (1755)</li>
					<li><strong>Johann Friedrich Agricola</strong>, <em>Anleitung zur Singkunst</em> / <em>Introduction to the Art of Singing</em> (1757, ed. Julianne C. Baird, 1995)</li>
					<li><strong>Giambattista Mancini</strong>, <em>Pensieri, e riflessioni pratiche sopra il canto figurato</em> (1774)</li>
					<li><strong>Johann Adam Hiller</strong>, <em>Anweisung zum musikalisch-zierlichen Gesange</em> (1780)</li>
					<li><strong>Domenico Corri</strong>, <em>The Singer's Preceptor</em> (c. 1810, Vols. I y III)</li>
					<li><strong>Giacomo Ferrari</strong>, <em>Breve compendio sul canto</em> (1818)</li>
					<li><strong>Richard Mackenzie Bacon</strong>, <em>Elements of Vocal Science</em> (1824)</li>
					<li><strong>Nicola Vaccai</strong>, <em>Metodo pratico di canto italiano per camera</em> (1832)</li>
					<li><strong>Luigi Lablache</strong>, <em>Méthode complète de chant</em> / <em>Complete Method of Singing</em> (c. 1840)</li>
					<li><strong>Manuel García II</strong>, <em>Traité complet de l'art du chant</em> / <em>A Complete Treatise on the Art of Singing</em> (1840–1847) y <em>Hints on Singing</em> (1894)</li>
					<li><strong>Gilbert-Louis Duprez</strong>, <em>L'Art du chant</em> (1845)</li>
					<li><strong>John Barnett</strong>, <em>School of Singing</em> (1845)</li>
					<li><strong>Giuseppe Concone</strong>, <em>50 Leçons de chant, Op. 9</em> (c. 1848)</li>
					<li><strong>Mathilde Marchesi</strong>, <em>Theoretical and Practical Vocal Method, Op. 31</em> (1890)</li>
					<li><strong>Francesco Lamperti</strong>, <em>The Art of Singing</em> (1890)</li>
				</ul>
			</section>

			<section>
				<h2 class="biblio-h2">2. Pedagogía vocal del siglo XX y XXI</h2>
				<ul class="biblio-list">
					<li><strong>Lilli Lehmann</strong>, <em>How to Sing (Meine Gesangskunst)</em> (1902)</li>
					<li><strong>David C. Taylor</strong>, <em>The Psychology of Singing</em> (1908)</li>
					<li><strong>Enrico Caruso &amp; Luisa Tetrazzini</strong>, <em>Caruso and Tetrazzini on the Art of Singing</em> (1909)</li>
					<li><strong>P. Mario Marafioti</strong>, <em>Caruso's Method of Voice Production: The Scientific Culture of the Voice</em> (1922)</li>
					<li><strong>Salvatore Fucito &amp; Barnet J. Beyer</strong>, <em>Caruso and the Art of Singing</em> (1922)</li>
					<li><strong>Giovanni Battista Lamperti</strong> (recop. William Earl Brown), <em>Vocal Wisdom: Maxims of Giovanni Battista Lamperti</em> (1931)</li>
					<li><strong>Victor Alexander Fields</strong>, <em>Training the Singing Voice</em> (1947)</li>
					<li><strong>E. Herbert-Caesari</strong>, <em>The Voice of the Mind</em> (1951, prólogo de Beniamino Gigli e introducción de Noel Bonavia-Hunt) y <em>The Alchemy of Voice</em> (1965)</li>
					<li><strong>William Vennard</strong>, <em>Singing: The Mechanism and the Technic</em> (1967)</li>
					<li><strong>Anthony Frisell</strong>, <em>The Baritone Voice</em> (1972)</li>
					<li><strong>James C. McKinney</strong>, <em>The Diagnosis and Correction of Vocal Faults</em> (1982)</li>
					<li><strong>Cornelius L. Reid</strong>, <em>A Dictionary of Vocal Terminology: An Analysis</em> (1983)</li>
					<li><strong>Richard Miller</strong>, <em>The Structure of Singing</em> (1986), <em>Training Tenor Voices</em> (1993), <em>On the Art of Singing</em> (1996), <em>National Schools of Singing</em> (1997), <em>Singing Schumann</em> (1999), <em>Training Soprano Voices</em> (2000), <em>Solutions for Singers</em> (2004), <em>Warm-Ups the Richard Miller Way</em> (2005) y <em>Securing Baritone, Bass-Baritone, and Bass Voices</em> (2008)</li>
					<li><strong>Barbara M. Doscher</strong>, <em>The Functional Unity of the Singing Voice</em> (1994)</li>
					<li><strong>Meribeth A. Dayme</strong>, <em>Dynamics of the Singing Voice</em> (2009)</li>
					<li><strong>Jennifer Hamady</strong>, <em>The Art of Singing on Stage and in the Studio</em> (2009)</li>
					<li><strong>Wendy LeBorgne &amp; Marci Daniels Rosenberg</strong>, <em>The Vocal Athlete</em> (2014)</li>
					<li><strong>Claudia Friedlander</strong>, <em>Complete Vocal Fitness: A Singer's Guide to Physical Training, Anatomy, and Biomechanics</em> (2018)</li>
					<li><strong>Janice L. Chapman &amp; Ron Morris</strong>, <em>Singing and Teaching Singing: A Holistic Approach to Classical Voice</em> (4.ª ed., 2023)</li>
				</ul>
			</section>

			<section>
				<h2 class="biblio-h2">3. Ciencia de la voz, acústica vocal y anatomía</h2>
				<ul class="biblio-list">
					<li><strong>D. Ralph Appelman</strong>, <em>The Science of Vocal Pedagogy: Theory and Application</em> (1967)</li>
					<li><strong>Johan Sundberg</strong>, <em>The Science of the Singing Voice</em> (1987)</li>
					<li><strong>Ingo R. Titze</strong>, <em>Principles of Voice Production</em> (1994)</li>
					<li><strong>Ingo R. Titze &amp; Katherine Verdolini Abbott</strong>, <em>Vocology: The Science and Practice of Voice Habilitation</em> (2012)</li>
					<li><strong>Kenneth Bozeman</strong>, <em>Practical Vocal Acoustics</em> (2013)</li>
					<li><strong>Theodore Dimon</strong>, <em>Anatomy of the Voice: An Illustrated Guide</em> (2018)</li>
				</ul>
			</section>

			<section>
				<h2 class="biblio-h2">4. Dicción, ornamentación y práctica interpretativa histórica</h2>
				<ul class="biblio-list">
					<li><strong>Luigi Ricci</strong>, <em>Variazioni, Cadenze e Tradizioni per Canto</em> (Ricordi, 1937)</li>
					<li><strong>Pierre Bernac</strong>, <em>The Interpretation of French Song</em> (1970)</li>
					<li><strong>Thomas Grubb</strong>, <em>Singing in French: A Manual of Diction and Technique</em> (1979)</li>
					<li><strong>Joan Wall et al.</strong>, <em>Diction for Singers: A Concise Reference</em> (1990)</li>
					<li><strong>Timothy J. McGee et al.</strong>, <em>Singing Early Music: The Pronunciation of European Languages in the Late Middle Ages and Renaissance</em> (1996)</li>
					<li><strong>Martha Elliott</strong>, <em>Singing in Style: A Guide to Vocal Performance Practices</em> (2006)</li>
					<li><strong>Philip Gossett</strong>, <em>Divas and Scholars: Performing Italian Opera</em> (2006)</li>
					<li><strong>Robert Toft</strong>, <em>Bel Canto: A Performer's Guide</em> (2013) y <em>With Passionate Voice: Re-Creative Singing in Sixteenth-Century England and Italy</em> (2014)</li>
				</ul>
			</section>

			<section>
				<h2 class="biblio-h2">5. Historia del canto, musicología y testimonios de intérpretes</h2>
				<ul class="biblio-list">
					<li><strong>Clara Kathleen Rogers</strong>, <em>The Philosophy of Singing</em> (1893)</li>
					<li><strong>William James Henderson</strong>, <em>The Art of the Singer: Practical Hints about Vocal Technics and Style</em> (1906)</li>
					<li><strong>Donald J. Grout &amp; Claude V. Palisca</strong>, <em>Historia de la Música Occidental</em> (Vols. 1 y 2, 1960 / ed. rev. 2001)</li>
					<li><strong>Rodolfo Celletti</strong>, <em>Le grandi voci: Dizionario critico-biografico</em> (1964), <em>Memorie d'un ascoltatore</em> (1985), <em>A History of Bel Canto</em> (1991) y <em>Grandi voci alla Scala</em> (1991)</li>
					<li><strong>Jerome Hines</strong>, <em>Great Singers on Great Singing</em> (1982)</li>
					<li><strong>John Potter</strong>, <em>Vocal Authority: Singing Style and Ideology</em> (1998)</li>
					<li><strong>James Stark</strong>, <em>Bel Canto: A History of Vocal Pedagogy</em> (1999)</li>
					<li><strong>Mary Jane Phillips-Matz</strong>, <em>Leonard Warren, American Baritone</em> (2000)</li>
					<li><strong>John Potter &amp; Neil Sorrell</strong>, <em>A History of Singing</em> (2012)</li>
					<li><strong>Gretchen Erlichman</strong>, <em>Bel Canto: The Beauty of the Past in the Voice of the Present</em> (Studienforum Berlin, 2013)</li>
					<li><strong>Salvador Ginori Lozano</strong>, <em>El arte del canto: Terminología sobre técnica vocal de los tratados de canto de los castrados y su relación con métodos de canto del siglo XIX</em> (Universidad Michoacana de San Nicolás de Hidalgo, 2024)</li>
				</ul>
			</section>
		</div>
	</div>
</Layout>

<style>
	.biblio-h2 {
		font-size: 1.48rem;
		color: #0f172a;
		padding-bottom: 0.45rem;
		margin-bottom: 1rem;
		border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border-color);
	}

	.biblio-list {
		list-style-type: disc;
		list-style-position: outside;
		padding-left: 1.45rem;
		margin: 0;
		display: flex;
		flex-direction: column;
		gap: 0.55rem;
	}

	.biblio-list li {
		display: list-item;
	}

	.biblio-list em {
		font-style: italic;
	}
</style>
